Z||000000||opm2000||03-05-2001||06:07 AM||||When I first found this forum, I stumbled across a few photos of a wooden framework someone built to lift Fiero rear ends for engine swaps.   Does anyone know where those photos are?   I've done about 4 swaps using the floor jack method, and that's getting pretty old.   I could go ahead without the pics, but you know...a picture is worth a thousand words.<P>David Breeze<BR>N777H||||reg||5
Z||000001||SteveJ||03-06-2001||09:05 AM||||Wooden? <P>Archie has steel. <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/v8rm1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/v8rm1.htm</A> <P>. . .but I haven't seen wood. A shame too 'cause I have a pile of 4x4's here too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||dman||03-06-2001||07:09 PM||||Hello everyone. Gene Down posted some pics of his fiero and his 3800SC engine swap. Here's one pic of his wooden "crane":<BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/gene-down/crane.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/gene-down/crane.jpg</A> <P>May that pic will help?<P>One tip (which you probably already know) is to slide the cradle out the side instead of from behind; you won't need to raise the rear end nearly as high. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||SteveJ||03-06-2001||08:33 PM||||Couple of pictures of his crane on the website - thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MontanaFiero||03-06-2001||09:34 PM||||Here are some recent pictures of my remov al. I just put a 4X4 post under the jacking points of my car and lifted it with a jack on each side. The cradle is sitting on a pallet with six  2 1/2 inch casters mounted to the bottom. That's it. See my thread.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005930.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005930.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||2
Z||000005||opm2000||03-06-2001||10:33 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by dman:<BR>[B]Hello everyone. Gene Down posted some pics of his fiero and his 3800SC engine swap. Here's one pic of his wooden "crane":<BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/gene-down/crane.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/gene-down/crane.jpg</A> <P>Yep, that's it!<BR>Thanks for the info.<BR>Like I said, after having gone thru the "jacking up" method on four different fiero projects, I really want the extra security of a crane.   There is a lot of potential for problems when jacking a Fiero on two floor jacks & a 4X4, although it does work.<P>David Breeze<P>||||reg||14
Z||000006||SteveJ||03-07-2001||09:24 AM||||Years ago, during an engine swap,  I had a car fall on me so I get a bit nervous when I put any part of my body under a car. Only a couple of concrete blocks I had put under for safety saved me. I had jacked up the car by putting block upon block kind of like MontanaFiero but stacked higher. It had looked stable. Some bolt was stubborn and I was pulling laterally. . . It fell in slow motion.<P>Thus my interest in a hoist. I have used the garage rafters in the past but this spring I need to swap the transmission in one of the family's other cars, a Buick. Most likely the engine and trans in one piece out the top, kind of heavy.<P>I like that wooden crane but I think I would have to use an "A" frame on the ends like Archie did using 4x4's. That would prevent a tipover better. <P>That 10" crossbar is a good idea as are the wheels at the bottom. How do we prevent it racking sideways?<P>Cost of materials is significant unless you have some lumber lying about.<P>Advance Auto has a hoist made in China for $219 which folds neatly for storage.. Autozone has one made in South Carolina for the same $219. Pepboys sells the South Carolina hoist for $249 ( might be a different model, I didn't check )<P>So if the cost of building one of these is any significant percentage of $219 we are probably better off with the steel hoist.<P>Drop that engine just once and the cost will exceed $219.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Archie||03-07-2001||12:05 PM||||Think Safety, & you'll be here long after your project is complete<P>Here is mine at work.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-664s.jpg"> ||||reg||1
